                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0658ca7c-2641-3211-8fce-08968e1adb5d",
                        "entry_id": "0b61cc9d-38fa-3d16-ade1-4c07a0934861",
                        "glosses": [
                            "отсутствие воздержания, неумеренность в чём-либо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9436fb10-5df7-49da-936c-6a81acf83ebe",
                                "sense_id": "0658ca7c-2641-3211-8fce-08968e1adb5d",
                                "text": "Собственным примером, а не запрещением изгнал он из полку карты, невоздержание, разврат."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c40f6f59-a2bc-3fe5-871e-7522dad9ad32",
                        "entry_id": "0b61cc9d-38fa-3d16-ade1-4c07a0934861",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. то же, что невоздержанность"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "358deddc-fbb5-4e87-b044-5056c3b65d7f",
                                "sense_id": "c40f6f59-a2bc-3fe5-871e-7522dad9ad32",
                                "text": "Итак, двадцать медных копеек избавили миролюбивого человека от следствия, детей моих от примера невоздержания во гневе, и я узнал, что рассудок есть раб нетерпеливости."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "86c02351-b957-43a6-ae64-19f5ad0b72f8",
                        "source_entry_id": "0b61cc9d-38fa-3d16-ade1-4c07a0934861",
                        "source_sense_description": "неумеренность",
                        "target_lang_word": "intemperance",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "intemperance",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9739bd2d-82be-3e24-b9da-e3ec07b40ac0",
                                        "entry_id": "d4d0eba0-0725-3cee-a328-b6ebbe7427da",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Lack of moderation or temperance; excess."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0ff4b86-6417-48d9-9ca6-d9f10d1c1e58",
                                                "sense_id": "9739bd2d-82be-3e24-b9da-e3ec07b40ac0",
                                                "text": "They deserved the enmity of the Pagans; and some of them might deserve the reproaches of avarice and intemperance; of avarice, which they gratified with holy plunder, and of intemperance, which they indulged at the expense of the people, who foolishly admired their tattered garments, loud psalmody, and artificial paleness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae0a6d9d-c1af-4695-860d-4e9dd045a50a",
                                                "sense_id": "9739bd2d-82be-3e24-b9da-e3ec07b40ac0",
                                                "text": "Raffles proved more unmanageable than he had shown himself to be in his former appearances, his chronic state of mental restlessness, the growing effect of habitual intemperance, quickly shaking off every impression from what was said to him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "12637207-a1cd-3c47-a505-51d5e0988dba",
                                        "entry_id": "d4d0eba0-0725-3cee-a328-b6ebbe7427da",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Drunkenness or gluttony."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8c0be40-3ef2-4ee1-8293-b437d55de7af",
                                                "sense_id": "12637207-a1cd-3c47-a505-51d5e0988dba",
                                                "text": "As I supported him towards his lodgings I could see that he was not only suffering from the effects of a recent debauch, but that a long course of intemperance had affected his nerves and his brain. […] He rambled in his speech, too, in a manner which suggested the delirium of disease rather than the talk of a drunkard."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50375d9b-4ce3-4bfa-b961-c3d0b4e81ec3",
                                                "sense_id": "12637207-a1cd-3c47-a505-51d5e0988dba",
                                                "text": "How can we marvel that the constitution thus disposed to intemperance finds the stimulus of drink indispensable?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b262b8a4-e763-4b3b-bb10-bc59e906ea39",
